[?2004l[?2004h>         "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "The safety risks listed for Paxlovid include: 1) Most common adverse reactions (incidence \u22651% and greater than placebo) from clinical trials: dysgeusia (5% vs. <1%) and diarrhea (3% vs. 2%). 2) Adverse reactions identified during Emergency Use Authorization (EUA) use: anaphylaxis, hypersensitivity reactions, toxic epidermal necrolysis, Stevens-Johnson syndrome, headache, hypertension, abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, and malaise. 3) Serious warnings/precautions: risk of serious adverse reactions due to drug interactions (especially with calcineurin inhibitors and calcium channel blockers), hepatotoxicity (transaminase elevations, clinical hepatitis, jaundice), and risk of HIV-1 resistance development in patients with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection.", M[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[K,
