[?2004l[?2004h>         }
[?2004l[?2004h>     },
[?2004l[?2004h>     {
[?2004l[?2004h>         "qid": "b54c25890c1ae3a6",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "Paxlovid should be administered orally, with or without food, at approximately the same time each day. All tablets in a dose (nirmatrelvir and ritonavir) must be taken together. The tablets must be swallowed whole and not chewed, broken, or crushed. If a dose is missed within 8 hours of the usual time, the patient should take it as soon as possible and resume the normal schedule. If missed by more than 8 hours, the patient should skip the missed dose and take the next dose at the regularly scheduled time (do not double the dose to make up for a missed dose). The full 5-day course must be completed.",
