[?2004lde", "carb[?2004h>         "answer": "Paxlovid (nirmatrelvir co-packaged with ritonavir) has significant drug interactions because ritonavir is a strong CYP3A inhibitor. Co-administration of Paxlovid with drugs primarily metabolized by CYP3A can increase plasma concentrations of these medications, potentially leading to severe, life-threatening, or fatal events. Conversely, co-administration with strong CYP3A inducers can significantly decrease nirmatrelvir and ritonavir concentrations, leading to a loss of therapeutic effect and potential viral resistance. Clinically serious interactions are commonly reported with calcineurin inhibitors (e.g., tacrolimus, cyclosporine) and calcium channel blockers.",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "citations": [
