[?2004l[?2004h>         "qid": "fbab4114f66e2dda",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "The important warnings and precautions associated with Paxlovid are: 1) Risk of Serious Adverse Reactions Due to Drug Interactions: Ritonavir is a strong CYP3A inhibitor, and co-administration with CYP3A-metabolized drugs can lead to serious, life-threatening, or fatal events, while strong CYP3A inducers can decrease Paxlovid exposure, causing loss of efficacy and resistance. 2) Hypersensitivity Reactions: Anaphylaxis, serious skin reactions (including toxic epidermal necrolysis and Stevens-Johnson syndrome), and other hypersensitivity reactions have been reported. 3) Hepatotoxicity: Hepatic transaminase elevations, clinical hepatitis, and jaundice have occurred in patients receiving ritonavir. 4) Risk of HIV-1 Resistance Development: Ritonavir co-administration may lead to HIV-1 developing resistance to HIV protease inhibitors in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection.",
