[?2004l[?2004h>     {
[?2004l[?2004h>         "qid": "c4dc176c4827f0ef",
[?2004l {[?2004h>         "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "Paxlovid should not be taken by: 1) Patients with a history of clinically significant hypersensitivity reactions (e.g., toxic epidermal necrolysis or Stevens-Johnson syndrome) to nirmatrelvir, ritonavir, or any other components of Paxlovid. 2) Patients taking any contraindicated medications, including those primarily metabolized by CYP3A for which elevated concentrations cause serious/life-threatening reactions, or strong CYP3A inducers. 3) Patients with severe hepatic impairment (Child-Pugh Class C), as Paxlovid is not recommended for use in this population due to a lack of pharmacokinetic or safety data.",
