[?2004l[?2004h>     {
[?2004l[?2004h>         "qid": "000ecd1d6df50389",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "The recommended dosage regimen of Paxlovid is: 1) Standard dosage for patients with normal renal function or mild renal impairment (eGFR >= 60 mL/min): 300 mg nirmatrelvir (two 150 mg tablets) with 100 mg ritonavir (one 100 mg tablet) taken together orally twice daily (morning and bedtime) for 5 days. 2) Patients with moderate renal impairment (eGFR >= 30 to <60 mL/min): 150 mg nirmatrelvir (one 150 mg tablet) with 100 mg ritonavir (one 100 mg tablet) taken together orally twice daily for 5 days. 3) Patients with severe renal impairment (eGFR <30 mL/min), including those requiring hemodialysis: Day 1: 300 mg nirmatrelvir (two 150 mg tablets) with 100 mg ritonavir (one 100 mg tablet) once. Days 2-5: 150 mg nirmatrelvir (one 150 mg tablet) with 100 mg ritonavir (one 100 mg tablet) once daily. On dialysis days, the dose should be administered after hemodialysis. The 5-day treatment course should be initiated as soon as possible after diagnosis of COVID-19, and within 5 days of symptom onset.",
